<title>USA: GCR says Q1 loss ratio 20.5 pct vs 31.0.</title>
<headline>GCR says Q1 loss ratio 20.5 pct vs 31.0.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>GCR Holdings said Friday its loss ratio in the fiscal first quarter was 20.5 percent, down from 31.0 percent a year earlier.</p>
<p>Loss ratio compares the ratio of losses and loss expenses to earned premium, the Hamilton, Bermuda-based insurer said.</p>
<p>It said that for the first quarter, ended December 31, its losses and loss expenses were $6.2 million, down from $10.2 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>The company said its loss experience is favorable by industry standards, and in the quarter there were no significant catastrophic events.</p>
</text>
